  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates a QSVM with quantum feature maps for fraud detection on a heavily reduced dataset (1500 train / 1000 test, 7 qubits). The QSVM achieves ~0.78 accuracy and ~0.81 AUC on a statevector simulator, comparable to classical XGBoost (~0.78–0.80 accuracy). A hybrid ensemble of QSVM and XGBoost reaches ~0.81 accuracy, while noisy simulation reduces QSVM accuracy to ~0.55.",
